# Dropbox Bulk Signup Automation — Project Overview

## 📌 One-Liner
A Node.js web dashboard that automates mass registration of Dropbox accounts using Playwright (Firefox), with multi-tier IP rotation (Direct → Cloudflare Warp → Psiphon → Socks5), browser fingerprint anti-detection, and automatic Dropbox daemon linking.

---

## 🏗️ Architecture Overview

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    Browser UI                        │
│              public/index.html + index.css           │
│                  (React-free vanilla JS)             │
├──────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┤
│   WebSocket Client   │   REST API Endpoints          │
│   (real-time sync)   │   /api/history,               │
│                      │   /api/uas,                   │
│                      │   /api/worker-stat,           │
│                      │   /api/settings/apply          │
├──────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┤
│                  server.js                            │
│  Express HTTP + WebSocket (ws) server                │
│  - Orchestrates batch registration                   │
│  - Broadcasts progress/logs to all connected clients │
│  - Manages worker idle/processing lifecycle          │
│  - Delegates per-email work to register.js           │
├──────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┤
│   register.js        │   db.js                       │
│  Playwright Firefox  │  JSON-file "database"         │
│  automation engine   │  (history.json)               │
│  - Proxy/VPN mgmt    │  - Registration records       │
│  - Browser fingerprint│ - Application settings        │
│    anti-detection     │                               │
│  - Dropbox daemon    │                               │
│    linking           │                               │
├──────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┤
│   fingerprint-check.js                                │
│  Diagnostic tool for inspecting browser fingerprints  │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

